  {
    "knowledge_id": "7d4be082-a247-55fa-ab19-b6c1bde66b5c",
    "collection_name": "project_6a04def407f04c709573821e59b571bb",
    "source_locator": "88accdb6-5587-583b-8f45-2e858d2703b9#page=8",
    "content": "Participants  consistently  highlighted  the  lack  of  industryspecific  ethical  standards  addressing  transparency,  inclu -sivity,  accountability,  labour  transformation,  and  cultural representation. Although ethical AI governance frameworks are  increasingly  discussed  in  broader  technology  sectors, the  findings  indicate  that  fashion  presents  unique  ethical challenges due to its symbolic, cultural, and creative characteristics. These results underscore the necessity for governance models that extend beyond technical regulation to include  social,  cultural,  and  creative  considerations  in AI implementation. The study thus advocates for collaborative governance approaches involving fashion organisations, AI developers,  policymakers,  and  educational  institutions  to establish context-sensitive ethical standards for AI adoption in the fashion sector.",
